The given function integrates to 2 over the support \([0,1] \times [0,2]\), so the properly normalized joint probability density function is \(f^*(x,y) = \frac{2x+2+y}{8}\). Using this valid density:

The probability that \(X + Y \ge 1\) is \(1 - P(X+Y < 1)\). The region where \(X+Y < 1\) within the support is \(0 \le y \le 1\), \(0 \le x \le 1-y\).

\[
P(X+Y < 1) = \int_0^1 \int_0^{1-y} \frac{2x+2+y}{8} \,dx\,dy = \frac{3}{16}
\]

Thus,

\[
P(X+Y \ge 1) = 1 - \frac{3}{16} = \frac{13}{16}
\]

